{
  "id": "ss.relic.berserk",
  "name": "Last sting",
  "description": "A sting torn out of the body that used it, sac and all: a long barbed needle running from a dark, wet venom sac at the top left to a point at the bottom right, three strands of red tissue still trailing off the sac where it came away, and a bead at the tip. A bee's sting is the hit it dies for — it costs the whole body and lands harder than anything else it can do — and that is the relic exactly: the nearer you are to dying, the harder you hit. The barbs are what keep the needle from reading as a thorn or a pin, so they are large and pale against it; a thorn is smooth, and a hooked needle is something that was meant to stay in. The sac is drawn as a gland rather than a bulb — a first pass with a round pale sac on the shaft read as a matchstick — and the strands hang limp instead of radiating, because tissue tears, it does not spark.",
